eaders or the viewers  or whatever has a reason to believe in  Trust  like reads out this prophecy or finds  out it's something that's guiding the  actions of somebody villains or Heroes  and then just scoffs crumples it up and  throws it away you're like  that's just some random nonsense  somebody wrote down  Because unless you justify why this is  correct  yeah it's some random nonsense somebody  wrote down  and again some things do engage a little  bit or at least try and create within  their settings a reason why the source  is something to be believed but much  like not needing to justify the actions  of your hair anymore once they are  designated protagonist by default a lot  will just not bother  the word prophecy comes up and because  of the narrative way in which prophecies  are used I.E to lay out how things are  supposed to go from here on out with  only the slight variations that I talked  about already then there's just an  expectation that the audience they know  how prophecies work we've told them this  is a prophecy doing a prophecy story now  but that's a meta-justification so if  you bother to actually justify and  grapple with it in Universe in narrative  so again it feels like a means to skip a  lot of steps to gloss over a lot of  stuff and I'm not even going to say that  that is an inherently bad thing because  sometimes if you're telling a certain  story there are certain things that just  don't interest you as a Storyteller that  you don't want to have to deal with or  you can't figure out an interesting way  to justify and so you take a shortcut  and that's the thing for me in the end  chosen ones and prophecies feel like  shortcuts and I understand why shortcuts  exist and I'm not going to say there's  never a reason to use them  but when it seems like the shortcut gets  used over and over and over and over  again well that's just becoming just  another standard path isn't it  prophecies chosen ones they are  narrative tools that from my experience  are used in  frustratingly limited ways because there  are more things that could be done with  these than usually are but as with most  tropes generally once invoked there's a  very clear funnel that this story and  these characters are now going to go  down and it's one I've seen and read and  heard and am at this point very  very bored by I want to see a story that  unravels because the characters make  decisions that make sense to them not  because Destiny has put its hand on the  scale  when I was younger I had more of  appreciation of a sense of Destiny and  fate and it still can work especially if  you're going with a little bit of a  tragic angle because I can think back to  this is going to be a weird movie to  pull but I'll mention it anyway one of  the things I really enjoyed about seeing  Peter Jackson's King Kong in the theater  was that it played best assuming you  knew how the original King Kong went and  so there was a sense of tragic  inevitability to it  kind of in the way how Romeo and Juliet  starts by a narrator literally telling  you this will end in both characters  deaths so you already know where it's  going and so the tragedy comes in  watching people try to avoid this but  you know it's coming anyway and I did  once have an appreciation for that  I've lost it and maybe it's age  bitterness maybe it's you know having  spent enough time doing my own writing  to just see how much of a easy cheat it  can be if you don't seriously explore  the concepts but for whatever reason  I'm over it  I hear the word prophecy I see a  character functionally become a Chosen  One by structure of the narrative or by  re oftentimes by reveal of their past I  kind of check out mentally  I'm just bored  I've seen this story I played this game  and I'm not saying it was never good  but I'm done I'm over it  and maybe others are too  or maybe others deeply love Chosen One  stories and in the latter case I hope  you can now at least understand a little  better why I don't and again  I know I said it during the thing I'm  not saying there is no such thing as a  good chosen one story most tropes are  not a problem in and of themselves they  are a problem as they become standard as  they become common as they become  so clearly used the same way pretty much  every time with little variation or in  the case of this as we have entered the  area the era of trying to subvert chosen  when expect expectations very formulaic  deviations  I think that's the thing chosen ones  feel so played out to me at this point  that even if it tries to subvert the way  the chosen one story works I still feel  like I already know what that's going to  look like and I'd just rather not  I would just rather not  you know this is part of why when I sat  down eventually and wrote my own fantasy  novel uh linked to buy that in the  description I focused on what I  considered small people in a big world  because when you deal with prophecies  and chosen ones you are dealing with the  people who reshape  everything  you are dealing with the names that will  be remembered by history and I think  being tired of that is part of why when  I wrote dreams of fire I'm like I am  focusing on people who will never get  more than a tiny footnote in a history  book  because  ultimately they're not important from  any Grand historical or mythical  perspective  but they still have good stories to tell  that's where I'm at in  my hopes I can still find some enjoyment  of stories of grand figures  but if we could keep the chosen Oneness  out of that I'll have a better chance of  enjoying those things  so that's me  has anything that I've said made any  kind of sense to you are you where I'm  at are you somewhere else do you think  what I said makes no sense whatever your  thoughts are drop something down in the  comments and let us talk about it  patreon is what pays the bills enables  me to do this as my living spend my time  thinking about these things thinkin